        "subject": "LU-17000 obdclass: fix error pointer put in index backup",
        "message": "LU-17000 obdclass: fix error pointer put in index backup\n\nWhen lu_object_find_slice() fails, lustre_index_backup() leaves the\nerror pointer in \"parent\", turns backup off and falls through to the\nexit path, which puts the object under a plain \"if (parent)\".  An error\npointer is not NULL, so dt_object_put_nocache() is handed it and\ndereferences it.  Clear the variable on the error path.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 6ff16309a006 (\"LU-10193 osd-zfs: backup index object with plain format\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I69285c2baed03907438fca3a1f86e29a1bc2b8df\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/68603\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nReviewed-by: Andreas Krause US <akrause@nvidia.com>\nReviewed-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
